{
  "abstract": "Let $P$ be Boolean on 18 inputs, of real multilinear degree at most six, with $P(0)=0$, $P(e_i)=1$ for all $i$, and $P(1^{18})=1$. We show that $P$ cannot be written as a disjoint composition with exactly 13 nonempty inner blocks. This excludes one construction route toward the sensitivity-versus-degree problem. We use exact linear and integer count certificates for multiple nonsingleton blocks. The last shape, one six-input block and twelve singleton blocks, requires keeping track of how weights are distributed among slices conditioned on individual coordinates and pairs. Standard-library Python checkers are included. We also include a checker for the related nine-light, three-quadratic-block obstruction at 12 blocks.",
